    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d797">

                <pb facs="0746" n="740" sameAs="frus:frus1939v04/pg740"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">867N.01/1515a: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the Minister in Egypt</hi>
                        (<hi rendition="#italic">Fish</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1939-04-11T17:00:00-05:00">April 11, 1939—5 p.m.</date></dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>19. Please comment by telegraph on a press report that Dr. Weizmann, President of
                    the World Zionist Organization, has arrived in Cairo at the invitation of the
                    Egyptian Government, that the Egyptian Ambassador has brought from London new
                    British proposals for Palestine and that a new conference might be held looking
                    to a settlement of Jewish-Arab differences. The presence in Cairo is also
                    reported of the Emir Feisal<anchor n="53" xml:id="d797-f1"/> and Iraq and
                    Palestine delegates.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Hull</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d797-f1" n="53" xml:id="d797-f1-content">
                <p>Eldest son of Ibn Saud; Foreign Minister for Saudi Arabia.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
